VERDICT
====================================================================================================
  The DBI wall is real in the field relations (A1-A3) but it is NOT a cluster fix inside the framework's own window: at nu_0 <= 1.8e-4 the
  pinned core sits at nu ~ 0.1-0.5, the enhancement 1/sqrt(1-nu^2) adds at most a few percentage points, and the wall is not reached.
  Reaching the core residual needs nu_0 above the window's upper edge (the RAR-via-drain bound) and drives the core INTO the wall, where c_s -> 0
  and the density diverges: the EFT exit / core collapse of nbody stage 3, not a controlled closure.  The cluster core stays >= 65% open;
  the two fronts (a0(z) window, cluster core) are now cross-linked by nu_0 rather than independent.

